// DWARF - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// DWARF: the debugging information format, and this is a complete
// `.debug_info` unit -- unit_length, version 4, the abbreviation
// offset it compiles against, an eight-byte address size, and one
// DIE whose DW_AT_producer is a DW_FORM_string.
//
// The producer string is the greeting `Hello World!`, and
// unit_length is the count of everything after itself, which is how
// a reader knows whether to believe the rest.
//
// dwarf: 24 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 14 00 00 00 04 00 00 00 00 00 08 48 65 6C 6C 6F |...........Hello|   <- 0000
// 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 00                         | World!.|   <- 0010
